/P 119 0 R
/E (Since January 2025, the US Outbound Investment Security Program has prohibited Americans from investing in Chinese micro-chip, semiconductor and AI companies. In return, China has also shown increasing scrutiny on an already restricted Western investment.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Protectionism on both sides creates an arms race for technological development with no other precedents outside the Cold War. The Chinese VC for advanced technology start-ups included in its 15th Five Year Plan and the US stake acquisitions in AI, microchips and rare earths companies are some examples on how both countries are stimulating their own talent to develop breakthrough technology locally.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Fundamentally, what this creates is a technology bifurcation. For allocators, the critical distinction is between de-risking by restructuring China exposure without fully withdrawing funds, and full decoupling, which implies permanent exit. Markets are currently doing both simultaneously, and that ambiguity is itself a source of valuation uncertainty in any deal carrying China-linked revenue or supply chain exposure.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
