/P 123 0 R
/E (Trade policy has historically been a background condition for private capital, in that something that has affected portfolio companies at the margin but has rarely determined where investors chose to deploy. That era is over. The new tariff regime imposed by the Trump administration from Liberation Day in early 2025 onwards has transformed trade policy into one of the most deterministic structural forces shaping deal flow, portfolio valuations, and geographic capital allocation in private markets today. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
